hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27669","Haddathana al-Hasan ibn Musa and Affan, they both said: Haddathana Amr ibn Marzuq, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij informed me, he said: My grandmother, meaning the wife of Rafi' ibn Khadij, informed me, Affan said: from his grandmother, mother of his father, wife of Rafi' ibn Khadij, that Rafi' shot an arrow with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Uhud and the day of Khaybar, he said: I doubt, with an arrow in his thanduwah. Then he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pull out the arrow. He said: O Rafi', if you wish I shall pull out the arrow and the head together, and if you wish I shall pull out the arrow and leave the head, and I shall testify for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr. He said: O Messenger of Allah, rather pull out the arrow and leave the head, and testify for me on the Day of Resurrection that I am a martyr. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pulled out the arrow and left the head."
